(10436, '_transient_dash_4077549d03da2e451c8b5f002294ff51', '<div class=\"rss-widget\"><ul><li><a class=\'rsswidget\' href=\'https://wordpress.org/news/2017/03/wordpress-4-7-3-security-and-maintenance-release/\' title=\'WordPress 4.7.3 is now available. This is a security release for all previous versions and we strongly encourage you to update your sites immediately. WordPress versions 4.7.2 and earlier are affected by six security issues: Cross-site scripting (XSS) via media file metadata.  Reported by Chris Andrè Dale, Yorick Koster, and Simon P. Briggs. Control characte [&hellip;]\'>WordPress 4.7.3 Security and Maintenance Release</a> <span class=\"rss-date\">6 مارس, 2017</span><div class=\'rssSummary\'>WordPress 4.7.3 is now available. This is a security release for all previous versions and we strongly encourage you to update your sites immediately. WordPress versions 4.7.2 and earlier are affected by six security issues: Cross-site scripting (XSS) via media file metadata.  Reported by Chris Andrè Dale, Yorick Koster, and Simon P. Briggs. Control characte [&hellip;]</div></li><li><a class=\'rsswidget\' href=\'https://wordpress.org/news/2017/01/wordpress-4-7-2-security-release/\' title=\'WordPress 4.7.2 is now available. This is a security release for all previous versions and we strongly encourage you to update your sites immediately. WordPress versions 4.7.1 and earlier are affected by three security issues: The user interface for assigning taxonomy terms in Press This is shown to users who do not have permissions to use it. […] [&hellip;]\'>WordPress 4.7.2 Security Release</a> <span class=\"rss-date\">26 يناير, 2017</span><div class=\'rssSummary\'>WordPress 4.7.2 is now available. This is a security release for all previous versions and we strongly encourage you to update your sites immediately. WordPress versions 4.7.1 and earlier are affected by three security issues: The user interface for assigning taxonomy terms in Press This is shown to users who do not have permissions to use it. […] [&hellip;]</div></li></ul></div>', 'no'),
